// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 14 (Impl-S, Cohort Delta): the E-GC-IN-LANE
// store rule at the SFC boundary. A lane-backed SFC collection cannot
// be stored into a GC-managed holder: the collector cannot trace into
// lane memory, and the holder's release would free lane bytes as if
// they were heap. SFC collections live in their region's lane and die
// at its rewind — exactly the lane-backed list discipline.
// MUST FAIL TO COMPILE.

fn main() {
    morton list<int, dims=[4, 4]> m = morton_new(4, 4)
    list<any> xs = []
    xs.push(m)
    print("unreachable")
}
